      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sales/quoting process was a bit awkward. The sales guy came out to our residence and sat down with us and pulled out his laptop to show us the placement of the panels. Then he went on to talk about how Sunflow was accredited and all that by the CEC council. This information I already knew since I went on to CEC to find an installer as opposed to a retailer. He showed us a diagram of all the inverter and panel brands. He quoted us $4765 for a 6.6kw system after rebate ($3661), Risen panels and Solis inverter. I was a bit concerned about the price since it was lower than expected. I wanted to go consult the price with my sister and give him an answer by the end of the day but he wanted an answer on the spot otherwise he wouldn't give us the discounted price. Without the discounted price, the price would've been $6k+. Paid a $500 deposit.Prior to the installation process, we were told to get some tiles just in case they were broken during the installation process. I was concerned about this because my roof tiles weren't in production anymore (Pioneer Ranch). Ashlee, their client sales relationship manager, was really helpful in providing me with some secondhand building material suppliers and I was able to get some tiles.The installation was very streamlined, they came early in the morning ~7am and finished by 11:30-12pm. Apparently, they had a guy that specialised in roofing so that made me more relaxed about the install process. At the end they helped explain how the inverter works and precautions we should take in the event we ever have any electrical or roofing maintenance work done.",
